# Interview Monitor (AI Track)

Detects potential attention events during a video interview using the webcam.
It does NOT prove misconduct. Every event is an indicator for human review.

## How it works
- MediaPipe Face Landmarker (model file: face_landmarker.task) finds face and iris points.
- OpenCV opens the webcam, draws status text, and saves snapshots.
- If head turn / looking away / no face / multiple faces lasts longer than
  SUSPICIOUS_SECONDS, a snapshot is saved with the time and reason in its filename.

## Setup
```
pip install opencv-python mediapipe
```

## Run
```
python monitor.py
```
Type `y` to consent, press Q in the video window to quit. A session summary is printed.

## Settings (top of monitor.py)
- HEAD_TURN_LIMIT, GAZE_LIMIT: sensitivity
- SUSPICIOUS_SECONDS: how long before saving a snapshot
- COOLDOWN_SECONDS: gap between snapshots
- GRACE_SECONDS: short breaks allowed before the timer resets

## Note
Saved images go to `cheating_captures/` (do not commit this folder).
